; wornrelief.eval - a surface type's `relief` row names its texture SET's own
; relief, the record `AssetBaker models` and `wornblock` bake it at
; (Assets/WornSets.h, code-review C406). Judged by tools/EditorTest.py phase 25.
;
; The schema's per-kind default (0.055 / 0.045 / 0.08) used to stand there: the
; slider started at the wrong depth for every shipped set, and an editor save
; re-baked the set at it. Every type below binds a set whose relief is NOT that
; default, and the wall and floor ones bind it under ANOTHER id, so neither the
; old default nor a readout keyed on the type's own id can pass.
;
; EditorTest writes, before this runs (into its scratch world, never the real
; one):
;   [et_unlisted]  texture = et_nosuchset            - no record: the kind's
;                                                      default (0.055)
;   [et_tuned]     texture = wall_brick, relief = 0.07 - set, so a slider; it
;                                                      still names the set's own
;
; Each section opens the type editor the palette's way, prints the derived
; values (`typeset derived <key> = <v>`) and what the rows built.

logecho on
reset
echo --- wall ---
typeset dialog walls wall_cobblestone
typeset dialog derived
typeset dialog rows
typeset dialog off
echo --- floor ---
typeset dialog floors floor_cobblestone
typeset dialog derived
typeset dialog off
echo --- ceiling ---
typeset dialog ceilings ceiling_rock_porous
typeset dialog derived
typeset dialog off
echo --- unlisted ---
typeset dialog walls et_unlisted
typeset dialog derived
typeset dialog off
echo --- tuned ---
typeset dialog walls et_tuned
typeset dialog derived
typeset dialog rows
typeset dialog off
echo --- end ---
